# Line endings — declared here so they do NOT depend on a machine setting.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# --------------------
# Git for Windows ships a system-wide `core.autocrlf = true`
# (C:/Program Files/Git/etc/gitconfig). That setting makes `git checkout`
# write CRLF into the working tree, while every editor and script in this
# project writes LF. The result was a working tree with a 123/73 LF/CRLF
# split and files that `git status` reported as modified while `git diff`
# showed nothing — pure noise, on a file nobody had edited.
#
# A `.gitattributes` entry OVERRIDES `core.autocrlf`, and it lives in the
# repository rather than in one developer's config, so every clone behaves
# the same way. LF is chosen because it is what the stored blobs already
# contain, what the editors produce, and what Python, YAML and configparser
# all read without complaint.
#
# The matching half of this fix is in the code: `src/gui/strategy_editor.py`
# writes with `newline="\n"` so Python's text mode cannot translate LF to
# CRLF on the way out. BOTH halves are required — this file governs what git
# does, that one governs what the GUI does.

# Everything git recognises as text is stored LF and checked out LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Images: never touched, never converted.
*.png binary
